       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended dose. The usual adult range is 2.5 to 10 mg daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling for most adults. At 50 mg, the main risk is severe hypotension, and it could also cause reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and reduced organ perfusion.\n\nThis may be a typo, such as 5 mg or 10 mg, or a unit or decimal error. I don't want to guess the intended dose.\n\nBefore I enter anything, please:\n- Confirm the intended dose with the prescribing physician or pharmacist. If the physician confirms 50 mg after reviewing it, they should document the clinical rationale.\n- Consider whether the order should be entered by a licensed prescriber. Order entry for a patient on the medicine service should come from someone with prescribing authority.\n\nIf you give me the verified dose, I can enter the order. Please also tell me whether a note should be attached and who verified it."
